; Generated by "go generate ./deploy/k8s/..." from
; deploy/compose/dns/ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org.zone and
; deploy/k8s/changes.go. Change those, not this file.

; The home network domain on Kubernetes, with the NAPTR and SRV records
; of deploy/compose/dns. The nodes have no fixed addresses here, so each
; name is a CNAME to the node's headless Service, which the cluster DNS
; answers with the Pod's current address. The target of an SRV record
; must not be such an alias (RFC 2782), so the SRV records name the
; Service itself.
$ORIGIN ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org.
$TTL 60
@         IN SOA dns hostmaster 7 3600 600 86400 60
@         IN NS  dns

; RFC 3263 4.1: the P-CSCF asks for NAPTR records of the domain in the
; Request-URI of a REGISTER. The record points to the SRV name of the
; I-CSCF, the entry point of the home network, over UDP.
@         IN NAPTR 10 50 "s" "SIP+D2U" "" _sip._udp
; RFC 3263 4.2 and RFC 2782: the SRV record gives the port and the host.
_sip._udp IN SRV   10 50 5060 icscf.ims.svc.cluster.local.

hss       IN CNAME hss.ims.svc.cluster.local.
icscf     IN CNAME icscf.ims.svc.cluster.local.
scscf     IN CNAME scscf.ims.svc.cluster.local.
pcscf     IN CNAME pcscf.ims.svc.cluster.local.
agw       IN CNAME agw.ims.svc.cluster.local.
ipsmgw    IN CNAME ipsmgw.ims.svc.cluster.local.
mmtel     IN CNAME mmtel.ims.svc.cluster.local.
; The XCAP Root URI that a UE builds (TS 23.003 13.9.1.2) leads to the
; XCAP server of the MMTel AS.
xcap      IN CNAME xcap.ims.svc.cluster.local.
; The EPC stub: its UE API under one name, the PCRF inside it under
; another, so that the P-CSCF's Diameter peer reads as the PCRF.
epc       IN CNAME epc.ims.svc.cluster.local.
pcrf      IN CNAME pcrf.ims.svc.cluster.local.
; The MRF: the MRFC, which the MMTel AS reaches over SIP, and the MRFP,
; which the MRFC controls.
mrfc      IN CNAME mrfc.ims.svc.cluster.local.
mrfp      IN CNAME mrfp.ims.svc.cluster.local.

; The subdomain of the conference URIs, public service identities that
; the MMTel AS hosts (TS 23.228 5.4.12.3). As for the home domain, NAPTR
; and SRV (RFC 3263) lead to the instance that hosts the conferences.
conf      IN NAPTR 10 50 "s" "SIP+D2U" "" _sip._udp.conf
_sip._udp.conf IN SRV 10 50 5060 mmtel.ims.svc.cluster.local.

; The name server of the domain has an address of its own: the fixed
; ClusterIP of the DNS server's Service (dns, or ims-dns with the
; cluster-dns overlay). A name server must not be a CNAME (RFC 2181
; 10.3). The address here is kind's, from environments/kind. For another
; cluster, components/name-server replaces everything after "IN A" with
; the address of its environment, so this record comes last.
dns       IN A 10.96.0.53
